#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Lemma]
// #title[Notation]
Let $X$ be a $pi_1$-finite 1-type, let $x:X$ be a point and let $"Aut"_X (x)$ be its finite #link("00H6")[automorphism group]. Then the cardinality of $"Aut"_X (x)$depends only on the #local("00H5")[connected component] $|x|_0$.

#proof[
  _Taking the cardinality_ of a finite set amounts to evaluating a map $|\_|: "FinSet" -> NN$. Since the natural numbers are a set, we may use the universal property of the set truncation to obtain a unique map $f$, such that the following diagram commutes.
 #figure(diagram($
	X edge("rr", |"Aut"_X (\_)|,->) edge("d", |\_|_0, ->) &  & NN \
	||X||_0 edge("urr", f,  "-->")
$))
This completes the proof.
For a connected component $c : ||X||_0$ we write write $|"Aut"_X (c)| :-= f(c)$
]

